    },
    {
      "id": "b07dq8r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S FIRST LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Statement:",
      "id": "o51kmy9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "An object remains at rest or in uniform motion in a straight line unless acted upon by an external force.",
      "id": "qbq5lce"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This law is also known as the Law of Inertia. Inertia:",
      "id": "7u5iv1i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The tendency of an object to resist change in its state of motion.",
      "id": "xxkmwmv"
    },
    {
      "id": "zoqxecx",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Inertia"
    },
    {
      "id": "cbm8ipn",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Inertia of Rest",
        "Inertia of Motion",
        "Inertia of Direction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g6qudvz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NEWTON’S SECOND LAW OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Statement:",
      "id": "tyewqjp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The rate of change of momentum of an object is directly proportional to the applied force and takes place in the direction of force.",
      "id": "cifht0m"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Formula:",
      "id": "524trle"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "For every action, there is an equal and opposite reaction.",
      "id": "98x9rk8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Force = Mass × Acceleration F = ma",
      "id": "cbzxn10"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "SI Unit of Force = Newton",
      "id": "l9baghy"
    },
    {
      "id": "wuapfgz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MOMENTUM"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Momentum is the product of mass and velocity. Formula:",
      "id": "uzywkku"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Momentum = Mass × Velocity p = mv",
      "id": "pibu8xa"
    },
